battlefield 2042 dropped a bombshell on  us by revealing an awesome new game mode  letting players relive some of the  golden years  of battlefield's history the new mode is  officially called battlefield portal and  lets players create their own scenarios  and join custom servers that incorporate  guns maps and factions from different  battlefield games  in this video we're going to break down  everything you need to know about  battlefield 2042's new mode  if you want to stay in the know  including when the 2042 beta will happen  and what it looks like make sure to pop  a quick like and subscribe  because man i am telling you the news is  coming in hot  so let's dive in battlefield portal is a  first in the series  allowing players to enjoy maps from  battlefield games of the past with the  newest frostbite engine and added  touches  crafted by studio ripple effect formerly  known as dice la  the game specifically brought back to  life in portal are  battlefield 1942 battlefield bad company  2  and battlefield 3. so if you were hoping  to see some titans from 2142 or any of  the vietnam backdrops you are out of  luck for now at least  that being said all three of those games  have fan favorite locations included in  portal like  caspian border el alamine and eureka  harbor  portal allows you to remix elements from  all four battlefield games including  their characters  maps guns and vehicles into custom  experiences  but you can also change the rules of the  game allowing you to create game modes  that are completely new  battlefield portal will have custom  modes that players can dive into  as curated by the devs themselves  however  community created experiences seem to be  the biggest point of emphasis  think halo forge players can customize  different aspects of their game  regardless of whichever era those  elements are from  at a high level you can select tons of  variables including what guns  vehicles factions and maps are in your  custom match  and then you can get extremely granular  with attachments damage health and a lot  of other small tweaks  that's right if you want to pit the  germans from world war  ii against a bunch of expats from 2042  you  absolutely can the only thing you can't  do at this stage  is mix different factions on a single  team battlefield portal will have six  classic maps combined with the seven  all-out warfare maps meaning a total of  13 available to players at launch  which is nice to hear honestly give me  all the maps  it's important to note that not every  location from those past games will be  included in battlefield portal  only two from each game are there at  launch battlefield 1942 will bring back  el alamine one of the largest  battlefield maps of all time  and battle of the bulge bad company 2  will bring back eureka harbor and  valparaiso  and lastly battlefield 3 will bring  caspian border  and no shark canals the maps have been  updated running the latest version of  frostbite in battlefield 2042's engine  which means adding awesome elements like  extensive destruction to places that  never had it before such as 1942's  battle of the bulge on the other hand  you have maps like valparaiso from bad  company 2  that'll have different low tide versions  with expanded play area  and this is to help accommodate the  significantly larger  128 player lobbies being able to see  some of these iconic maps come to life  on next gen is extremely exciting and i  can't wait to see all three of those  games getting the current frostbite  engine makeover  the weapons vehicles and equipment will  be making a return  and all of their retouched next-gen  glory as well  vehicles returning are chosen by dice  but fans will be pleased to see  a much wider selection of their favorite  weapons or exotic ones like the xm8  worth mentioning too that the weapons  included are based on player data  and usage when you combine all of the  arsenal from these three remastered  games as well  as the content from the world of 2042  you have  over 40 vehicles 40 weapons and 30  gadgets  that is a lot of tools to unleash chaos  with on the battlefield  all of the maps will be playable in 4k  at 60 frames per second  and next gen platforms can enjoy the  added 128 player lobbies  ps4 and xbox one owners will still get  to enjoy the reimagined maps but with 64  player matches how will these matches be  balanced you may ask  they won't be developers stated that it  is up to the players to figure that out  and there are a lot of ways to do it  you can change a lot of core settings  like allowing early reloads adjusting  the damage multiplier  putting on friendly fire or even  changing the speed of projectiles  battlefield portal is wide open for the  most part in regards to the game's rules  except no special terrain editing so  what you can do  is change the parameters of any  battlefield match but you can't change  the integrity of the game for it to be  anything  that isn't a general battlefield match  so no  you cannot make your own custom battle  royale if that is what you were hoping  to do  if there's one thing that i have faith  in however it is the imagination of this  community  and coming up with experiences that will  be truly memorable  also kind of a big deal but there's a  logic editor  you'll be able to customize a game mode  and experience from scratch and if  you've got some script building skills  in your arsenal  there's very little limitations on what  you can create short of breaking the  game  one of the examples we saw at the  preview event was setting a script rule  in the logic editor where every time a  player got a kill  that same player was healed to full  health or  if you got a kill you can force weapons  to swap for everyone on the team  most of the logic editor stuff is way  too advanced for me  but i know some of y'all watching this  video are already cracking your knuckles  eager to get going and creating a truly  custom experience  here's something else super cool  battlefield portal will allow you to  level up  and gain xp as if you were playing a  regular all-out warfare game mode  usually when it comes to things like  custom servers or private matches  it's hard to gain xp if at all since  players can essentially  game the system there are safety nets of  sorts in battlefield portal that will  prevent players from abusing this model  to gain xp  but ripple effect says that progression  will work in portal  just as in other gameplay modes in short  the xp system in battlefield portal will  be more or less the same as that in  battlefield 2042  with the caveat that portal has certain  safeguards to protect itself  from players trying to take advantage  and speed up their xp gains  we got a look at the pre-alpha creation  menus and it seems  really intuitive most of the featured  experiences are really straightforward  like making a bad company 2 versus a  1942 type mode  but if you want to get really creative  you just go through a series of menus  clicking which options you want and that  snipers vs shotguns mode you wanted is  suddenly a reality  you can set up the game mode style that  you want be it conquest  conquest small rush or something  completely custom  you can choose the maps and the map  rotation from any number of classic or  2042 maps and you can mix and match  and you can even mess with things like  team distribution putting 100 players on  one team and only 28 on the other  to be completely honest with you  battlefield portal sounds like the game  mode i didn't know i needed  mainly because i didn't quite think it  was possible clearly  the developers have taken into account  just how passionate all of you are  about some of these older battlefield  games and they have taken the huge task  of recreating  all of those experiences from  battlefield's golden era so let me know  how you feel about battlefield portal  and which maps you're going to jump into  first  or if you're more excited to craft your  own distinct custom experience  also let me know if there are other maps  you hope to see in battlefield portal's  future  because ripple effect didn't quite  reveal much about what could be added in  the future  but they've mentioned that battlefield  portal is just the first step in the  beginning  of a larger journey they're always  looking to interact with the community  to find out what you guys might want to  see happen to portal over time  if you're excited and eager and just  can't wait to get your hands on  battlefield 2042  you'll get a chance to play the  battlefield beta this september  until then we'll see you next time  you
 

